.TH MODMAN-TUI 8 "2026-05-29" "modman" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
modman-tui - dialog terminal frontend for modman
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B modman-tui
[--help|--version]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B modman-tui
is an optional Bash + dialog frontend for the modman(8) backend. It is a
presentation layer only: every list and action goes through
.B modman --machine,
and filesystem/runtime work stays inside the backend and pfs-utils.
.PP
The TUI never calls pfs-utils, pacman, sudo, or pkexec directly, and it does
not parse human-readable modman output.
.SH MENU FLOWS
.TP
.B Connected modules
Runs modman --machine --list-loaded-after. Selected modules can be viewed or
detached after a dialog --yesno confirmation via modman --machine -R <name>.
.TP
.B System modules
Runs modman --machine --list-loaded-before. Selected modules can be viewed or
detached after confirmation via modman --machine -R <name>.
.TP
.B Local modules
Runs modman --machine --list-local. Selected modules can be attached via
modman --machine -S <path-or-name> or removed after confirmation via
modman --machine --remove-local <name...>. A file selector can attach a chosen
local file through the same backend install command.
.TP
.B Search
Prompts for a query and runs modman --machine -Ss <query>. Selected results
are installed only after confirmation with modman --machine -S.
.TP
.B Updates
Runs modman --machine --check-updates. Normal and loaded-risk updates are
selected by default; system-risk updates are off by default and require an
extra confirmation before --confirm-system-updates --update <id> is used.
Blacklist actions use only --update-blacklist-* backend commands.
.TP
.B Old cleanup
Runs modman --machine --list-old and accepts only backend old-file rows.
Removal requires confirmation and calls modman --machine --remove-old.
.TP
.B Settings / about
Displays read-only config path information and about text. It does not launch
an editor and does not call --open-config.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B MODMAN_BIN
Path to the backend executable. Defaults to the first modman in PATH.
.TP
.B DIALOG_BIN
Path to the dialog executable. Defaults to the first dialog in PATH.
.TP
.B MODMAN_TUI_TMPDIR
Temporary directory override, primarily for automated tests.
.SH FAILURE HANDLING
If a backend command is unavailable or emits an unsupported machine schema,
the TUI shows an unavailable-function message and returns to the previous
menu. Unsupported list commands never trigger follow-up mutation commands.
.SH SEE ALSO
modman(8), modman.conf(5), dialog(1)
